remarks.code:
[CVarContainer]
public static class FogCVars
{
    public static readonly NumericCVar<int> Quality =
        CVar.Int("r_fog_quality", 3, 0, 4, CVarOptions.Archive, "Volumetric fog quality: 0 off .. 4 ultra");
}

member.remarks:
A missing part is nought, so 1.2 is 1.2.0. A part that is not a number (1.2-beta's 2-beta)
is compared by its leading digits and then by its text, so a pre-release sorts after its number's release only by text;
mods that need more than that say so in their own numbering.

remarks.code:
c ^= a >> 7;   // logical shift
b ^= c;
a += b;
return (u16)a * (1 / 65536.0);

member.remarks:
Each component is divided by the length, which rounds differently from multiplying by its reciprocal; see
 for the code that does that instead. The test is length > minimumLength,
so a length that is not a number takes the fallback.
